---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import HiddenIcon from '../components/HiddenIcon.astro';
import NumberedList from '../components/NumberedList.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Pager from '../components/Pager.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import TextSection from '../components/TextSection.astro';
import WhereWorkGoes from '../components/WhereWorkGoes.astro';
import { citation, definition } from '../data/definition.ts';
import { hiddenFunctionIds, hiddenFunctions } from '../data/hidden-functions.ts';
import { questions } from '../data/questions.ts';
import { signs } from '../data/signs.ts';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { casesMissing } from '../lib/hidden-work.ts';

const cases = await getCollection('cases');

const contents = [
  { id: 'story', label: 'The story' },
  { id: 'hidden', label: 'The hidden work' },
  { id: 'questions', label: 'The three questions' },
  { id: 'right-call', label: 'When automation is the right call' },
  { id: 'reading', label: 'Further reading' },
] as const;
---

<Site
  title="The doorman fallacy"
  current="idea"
  description="Rory Sutherland's doorman fallacy: judging a job by its most visible task, and replacing the task, can remove the work nobody wrote down."
>
  <div class="page">
    <PageHead title="The doorman fallacy" lead={definition} contents={contents}>
      <div id="cite" class="cite">
        <p class="t-caption ink-2">How to cite</p>
        <p class="t-small">{citation}</p>
        <p class="t-small ink-2">
          The cases and this text are free to reuse under <ExternalLink href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</ExternalLink>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </PageHead>

    <TextSection id="story-title" anchor="story" number={1} title="The story">
      <p>
        Rory Sutherland tells it in his book <i>Alchemy</i> (2019). A hotel hires consultants to cut costs.
        They describe the doorman&rsquo;s job as opening the door, and an automatic door does that for less.
        So the doorman goes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The door still opens. But the doorman also greeted regular guests by name, found taxis in the rain,
        kept an eye on who came in, and told every arriving guest that this was a hotel that looked after
        people. None of that was in the job description, so none of it was counted when the decision was
        made. Its cost turns up later, somewhere else.
      </p>
      <p class="t-small ink-2">
        The idea and the story are Rory Sutherland&rsquo;s. <i>Alchemy: The Surprising Power of Ideas That
        Don&rsquo;t Make Sense</i>, 2019.
      </p>
      <h3 id="now-title" class="t-subhead">Why it matters now</h3>
      <p>
        AI can now do many visible tasks well: answer the customer&rsquo;s question, write the product text,
        screen the application. When a role is described by its visible task, the case for replacing it looks
        simple. The savings are counted on the task. The hidden work is not counted, because nobody listed
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site&rsquo;s view is practical. Use AI where it does the job. Before deciding, count everything
        the person did.
      </p>
    </TextSection>

    <TextSection id="hidden-title" anchor="hidden" number={2} title="The hidden work" full>
      <Photo slot="aside" id="portrait" sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 33vw, 100vw" />
      <p class="prose">Six kinds of work that disappear without being missed at first. For each: what it looked like at the hotel door, what it looks like today, how its loss shows, and the question to ask before the change.</p>
      <ul class="hidden-kinds">
        {
          hiddenFunctionIds.map((id) => {
            const kind = hiddenFunctions[id];
            const found = casesMissing(cases, id);
            return (
              <li id={id} class="hidden-kind ruled">
                <h3 class="hidden-kind__name t-subhead">
                  <HiddenIcon id={id} class="ink-2" />
                  {kind.label}
                </h3>
                <p class="ink-2">{kind.meaning}</p>
                <dl class="hidden-kind__facts">
                  <div>
                    <dt class="t-small ink-2">At the hotel</dt>
                    <dd>{kind.atTheHotel}</dd>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <dt class="t-small ink-2">Today, for example</dt>
                    <dd>{kind.today}</dd>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <dt class="t-small ink-2">When it goes missing</dt>
                    <dd>{kind.whenMissing}</dd>
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <dt class="t-small ink-2">The question to ask</dt>
                    <dd class="t-label">{kind.ask}</dd>
                  </div>
                </dl>
                <p class="hidden-kind__ledger t-small ink-2">
                  {found.length === 0 ? (
                    'No case in the ledger records this missing yet.'
                  ) : (
                    <>
                      In the ledger:{' '}
                      {found.map((item, index) => (
                        <>
                          {index > 0 && ' · '}
                          <a href={item.href}>{item.short}</a>
                        </>
                      ))}
                    </>
                  )}
                </p>
              </li>
            );
          })
        }
      </ul>
    </TextSection>

    <TextSection id="questions-title" anchor="questions" number={3} title="The three questions">
      <p>
        Three questions to ask before replacing a role. Each one rests on research from safety, economics and
        sociology, named under it.
      </p>
      <div slot="wide" class="questions">
        {
          questions.map(({ title, ask, parts }, index) => (
            <div class="question grid">
              <div class="question__head">
                <p class="section-number">Question {index + 1}</p>
                <h3 class="t-subhead">{title}</h3>
                <p class="ink-2">{ask}</p>
              </div>
              <ul class="question__parts">
                {parts.map((part) => (
                  <li class="question__part">
                    <p class="t-label">{part.title}</p>
                    <p>{part.detail}</p>
                    <ul class="question__sources t-small ink-2">
                      {part.sources.map(({ cite, href }) =>
                        href === undefined ? <li>{cite}</li> : <li><ExternalLink href={href}>{cite}</ExternalLink></li>,
                      )}
                    </ul>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))
        }
        <WhereWorkGoes />
        <div id="signs" class="question grid">
          <div class="question__head">
            <h3 id="signs-title" class="t-subhead">Signs of the mistake</h3>
            <p class="ink-2">A decision that shows several of these has answered the first question and skipped the other two.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="question__parts">
            <NumberedList items={signs} />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </TextSection>

    <TextSection id="right-call-title" anchor="right-call" number={4} title="When automation is the right call">
      <p>Sometimes the machine should take the task. Automating it is the right call when:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>The visible task really is the whole job: resetting a password, changing an address, tracking a parcel.</li>
        <li>The hidden work has been named, and someone has been given it on purpose.</li>
        <li>The hidden work is measured after the change, as well as the saving.</li>
        <li>The people who did the job helped design the change, and can say when it is not working.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The ledger records <a href="/ledger">cuts that held up</a> as faithfully as those that were reversed.</p>
    </TextSection>

    <TextSection id="reading-title" anchor="reading" number={5} title="Further reading">
      <ul class="reading">
        <li>
          <p>Rory Sutherland, <i>Alchemy: The Surprising Power of Ideas That Don&rsquo;t Make Sense</i> (2019).</p>
          <p class="ink-2">Where the doorman comes from.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>Lisanne Bainbridge, &ldquo;Ironies of Automation&rdquo; (1983).</p>
          <p class="ink-2">Why automating the routine work leaves people with the hardest part.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>Michael Polanyi, <i>The Tacit Dimension</i> (1966).</p>
          <p class="ink-2">&ldquo;We can know more than we can tell.&rdquo;</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>David Autor, &ldquo;Why Are There Still So Many Jobs?&rdquo; (2015).</p>
          <p class="ink-2">Jobs as bundles of tasks, and the tasks machines find hardest.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>Jerry Z. Muller, <i>The Tyranny of Metrics</i> (2018).</p>
          <p class="ink-2">What happens when the measure becomes the goal.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>James C. Scott, <i>Seeing Like a State</i> (1998).</p>
          <p class="ink-2">How simplified views of work lose what makes it work.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>Marilyn Strathern (1997), after Charles Goodhart (1975):</p>
          <p class="ink-2">&ldquo;When a measure becomes a target, it ceases to be a good measure.&rdquo;</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </TextSection>

    <Pager next={{ label: 'The ledger', href: '/ledger' }} />
  </div>
</Site>

<style>
  .cite {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    max-inline-size: 40em;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-4);
    border-block-start: var(--hairline) solid var(--rule);
  }

  /* The hidden work: one ruled entry per kind, its four facts in two columns on wider screens. */
  .hidden-kinds {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-12);
  }

  .hidden-kind {
    scroll-margin-block-start: var(--space-8);
  }

  .hidden-kind__name {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hidden-kind > * + * {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .hidden-kind__facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6) var(--grid-gap);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
  }

  .hidden-kind__facts dd {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-1);
    max-inline-size: var(--measure);
  }

  .hidden-kind > .hidden-kind__ledger {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (width >= 40rem) {
    .hidden-kind__facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  /* The three questions: each a row, the question on the left in the heading column, its ideas on the right. */
  .questions {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-8);
  }

  .question {
    row-gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-8);
    border-block-start: var(--hairline) solid var(--rule);
  }

  .question__head,
  .question__parts {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .question__head {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .question__parts {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    max-inline-size: var(--measure);
  }

  .question__part > * + * {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
  }

  .question__sources {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  @media (width >= 56rem) {
    .question__head {
      grid-column: 1 / span 4;
      padding-inline-end: var(--space-8);
    }

    .question__parts {
      grid-column: 5 / span 8;
    }
  }

  .reading {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
